From e10d462d2a8927a0c087e1fe04964f6f85eced59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel FORTE <gab@chx-labs.org>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:18:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] [Bugfix][Spec Decode] Let --hf-overrides RoPE scaling
 reach the MTP drafter

Dict hf_overrides were withheld from the draft ModelConfig on the grounds that
they patch one checkpoint's keys. That is right for a draft from another repo
and wrong for the common MTP case, where the draft config is built from the
target's own config.json: the target got the patch and the drafter read the
unpatched checkpoint. With RoPE scaling the drafter then built an unscaled
rotary embedding while the target used the scaled one, so the two disagreed on
every position past the original window, by 0.07 in max cos/sin difference at
position 1000, 1.36 at 100000 and 2.04 at 262143, and acceptance decayed
exactly where speculative decoding is supposed to help. All that showed in the
log was a second "Using max model len" line carrying the smaller number.

Forward dict overrides only when the draft model resolves to the target's own
checkpoint, and apply them before the architecture mapping, since that mapping
may hand back a nested sub-config that the keys no longer address.

That also lets RoPE standardization run against the Qwen4Exp wrapper, which
aliases text_config.rope_parameters and so counts as a RoPE-bearing config to
transformers: once the aliased dict declares a scaling type it reads the
trained window off the same object, and the wrapper never had one. Mirror the
text config's max_position_embeddings onto it.
